  "visualReview": {
    "coverage": "Viewed all 64 pages and 8 covers in eight 3×3 contact sheets, then re-inspected corrected sheets. Selected full-size views: 0201 p05 and p07; 0202 p07; 0203 p08; 0204 p08 and cover; 0205 p06 and p07; 0206 p05, p07 and p08; 0207 p03 and p08; 0208 p07 and p08.",
    "notes": [
      "0201: the fennec retains sand fur, oversized ears, white tail tip, blue vest and cream bag. A dry stone has no picture; wet patches show only the red tail, then one eye and two curves. The reverse holds water but has no picture. The completed fish and exactly three bubbles fit within the stone surface, and the final stone stays submerged in its shallow bowl on the window table.",
      "0202: one yellow flower pot moves from the visitor to the inner ledge and then to a low stone outside, away from the cave nose. Exactly two cups remain through every stage; the final cups belong to cave and hedgehog. Four table legs are visible, tea is poured into the table cup, and the nose-touching and pouring arms replace the default arms.",
      "0203: the red knitted scarf has eyes at one end, short fringes at both ends, and is never shown as its former yarn ball. Exactly two cushions form the attempted slope, then the two riverbanks. One rectangular block becomes the boat and ends on the mouse’s lap. The final scarf rests below the mouth and around the shoulders.",
      "0204: two heads share a visibly continuous green neck/body and blue pajamas. The left head has two gold horns and the right head two brown horns. The window stays on the right head’s side; open, closed and narrow-gap curtains are separate states. The cloth hangs on a wooden support between two pillows; the ending shows the host’s separate small bed. The cover keeps the moon inside its square crop.",
      "0205: the blue telescope has one brass toothed focus wheel and no arms. The observer’s hands turn the wheel, then move away for the clear view. The eyepiece inset progresses from diffuse white to a defined moon with craters; the glasses are off the face only while being wiped. A profile observer, visible stool and one continuous white-tipped tail clarify the final observing posture.",
      "0206: the wooden guest remains much smaller than the mouse. Cotton first fills the box, is reduced, and is then removed completely. The guest lies straight on the bare wooden floor before the empty box is inverted. On the hard bed the blanket leaves the face visible, the green pointed hat is beside the bed, and the final removed cotton belongs to the mouse’s soft nest.",
      "0207: the stone mushroom remains attached to the sheltered garden entrance in every view. Dirty path snow is rejected, the grass root is exposed once and covered again, and clean snow is carried from the wooden bench. The completed snow cap leaves both eyes visible; the final bench has a cleared seat while the flowerbed remains covered.",
      "0208: there is one cloud pillow and one fish picture book. The loss basket is genuinely empty when the pillow is carried away or reunited with its owner. The yellow handkerchief is removed before the return. The final pillow rests at the grandmother’s neck while the fox reads beside her, with no duplicate pillow in the basket or fox’s hands."
    ],
    "limits": "Simplified original vector picture-book style. Contact sheets check composition and continuity; selected pages are enlarged. This review does not include bitmap painting, audio QA, browser layout QA or child-user testing."
  },
